{
  "slug": "artist:dj-paul",
  "name": "DJ Paul",
  "editorial_article": "Born Paul Duane Beauregard in Memphis, Tennessee, DJ Paul began his career in 1988 at age 11 as a DJ at the local venue 380 Beale. In 1989, he formed the duo Serial Killaz with his half-brother, Lord Infamous, recording their earliest tapes using equipment rented with money from their father. Along with Juicy J, he helped pioneer the modern mixtape format by featuring original tracks from local artists rather than simple compilations. Together with Juicy J, he founded the group Three 6 Mafia and their label Hypnotize Minds, defining a sound characterized by dark, eerie, and bass-heavy production. In 2006, the group won an Academy Award for Best Original Song for 'It's Hard out Here for a Pimp' from the film Hustle & Flow. In 2018, Paul expanded his production work to the mainstream by co-producing the track 'Talk Up' for Drake's album Scorpion. Beyond music, he has managed diverse business ventures including a signature line of BBQ seasonings, a real estate company, and part-ownership of FaZe Clan.",
